WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:18.966
"What do you mean, your painting is gone?" Henry asked Nathan.

2
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:20.790
"Where did it go?"

3
00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:24.151
"I don't know." Nathan sounded upset.

4
00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:27.770
"That's what I need The Lemonade Detectives to figure out!"

5
00:00:27.771 --> 00:00:32.788
Cole handed him some lemonade. "Here, drink this," he said.

6
00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:35.105
"Then tell us what happened."

7
00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:38.083
Nathan gulped down the lemonade.

8
00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:42.204
"I wanted to get a snack before the judging started," he said.

9
00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:46.365
"I left the art show for a few minutes to go to the taco stand.

10
00:00:46.366 --> 00:00:50.089
When I got back, my painting was gone!"

11
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.307
"How could it just disappear?" Maggie asked.

12
00:00:53.308 --> 00:00:55.498
"There were all kinds of people around.

13
00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:58.102
Somebody must have seen what happened."

14
00:00:58.103 --> 00:01:02.768
Nathan shook his head. "Nora wandered off a little while ago.

15
00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:08.057
My mom went to look for her. So they weren't there when it disappeared."

16
00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:12.366
He looked upset. "Will you guys take the case?"

17
00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:17.736
"Of course," Henry said. "Let's go take a look at the scene of the crime."

18
00:01:17.737 --> 00:01:23.757
They closed the lemonade stand and walked over to the art show.

19
00:01:23.758 --> 00:01:26.956
The spot where Nathan's painting had hung was empty.

20
00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:31.765
Nathan bit his lip. "What do you think happened to my painting?"

21
00:01:31.766 --> 00:01:35.827
"That's what we need to find out." Henry looked around.

22
00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:39.004
There were other paintings hanging nearby.

23
00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:43.133
"Did you ask any of the other artists if they saw anything?"

24
00:01:43.134 --> 00:01:49.068
Nathan nodded. "There weren't many people nearby. Nobody saw a thing."

25
00:01:49.069 --> 00:01:52.625
"Why would someone steal a painting?" Maggie wondered.

26
00:01:52.626 --> 00:01:56.077
"Wait, I know! What about Patrick?"

27
00:01:56.078 --> 00:02:00.322
Henry nodded. "I was about to ask the same thing.

28
00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:03.290
Patrick seems suspicious to me."

29
00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:09.839
Cole nodded. "Patrick seemed mad when Owen told us what the judges said about Nathan's painting.

30
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.419
Patrick might be trying to knock out the competition."

31
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.491
Maggie clenched her fists. "Let's go talk to him!"

32
00:02:17.492 --> 00:02:20.960
"Wait." Henry turned to Nathan.

33
00:02:20.961 --> 00:02:24.980
"Has anyone else said anything about your painting?"

34
00:02:24.981 --> 00:02:28.744
Nathan shrugged. "Just Mr. Collins."

35
00:02:28.745 --> 00:02:32.080
"Mr. Collins?" Henry was surprised.

36
00:02:32.081 --> 00:02:35.867
Mr. Collins was a barber who entered the art show every year.

37
00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.828
"What do you mean?"

38
00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:42.862
"He noticed my painting earlier today and seemed kind of upset," Nathan said.

39
00:02:42.863 --> 00:02:46.527
"He says it's really similar to his painting."

40
00:02:46.528 --> 00:02:49.212
"Is it similar?" Henry asked.

41
00:02:49.213 --> 00:02:53.944
Nathan shrugged. "I don 't know. I haven't seen his painting."

42
00:02:53.945 --> 00:03:02.766
"What are we waiting for?" Maggie said. "Let's go check it out."

43
00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:06.108
It didn't take long to find Mr. Collins' painting.

44
00:03:06.109 --> 00:03:08.421
Cole wrinkled his nose when he saw it.

45
00:03:08.422 --> 00:03:12.628
"That doesn't look like your painting at all," he told Nathan.

46
00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:18.108
"Yeah," Maggie agreed. "It looks like a bunch of crazy cubes."

47
00:03:18.109 --> 00:03:21.612
A woman standing nearby heard them and looked over.

48
00:03:21.613 --> 00:03:25.397
"Are you talking about Mr. Collins' piece?" she asked.

49
00:03:25.398 --> 00:03:30.500
"It's wonderful, isn't it? He calls it Calico at Rest.

50
00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.757
He has such a way with the Cubist style!"

51
00:03:33.758 --> 00:03:40.012
"It's very nice," Henry said politely. Then he led his friends away.

52
00:03:40.013 --> 00:03:45.617
"I guess both paintings have calico cats. But they don't look alike."

53
00:03:45.618 --> 00:03:48.574
"That's for sure!" blurted out Maggie.

54
00:03:48.575 --> 00:03:52.323
"Mr. Collins is pretty sensitive," said Cole.

55
00:03:52.324 --> 00:03:55.525
"Maybe he thinks Nathan copied his idea."

56
00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:58.883
"But I didn't!" Nathan protested.

57
00:03:58.884 --> 00:04:03.166
"We know you didn't copy him," Henry assured Nathan.

58
00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:09.497
"But Mr. Collins might not. He should probably be on our suspect list."

59
00:04:09.498 --> 00:04:12.515
"And Patrick too, right?" Cole asked.

60
00:04:12.516 --> 00:04:18.162
"Definitely," Henry said. "Nathan and Patrick are in the same age category.

61
00:04:18.163 --> 00:04:22.509
That means Patrick has a better motive than Mr. Collins."

62
00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:27.915
Maggie was biting her lip, looking worried. "What about Hannah?" she said.

63
00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:30.467
"What about her?" Cole asked.

64
00:04:30.468 --> 00:04:35.728
"She got upset when we mentioned Nathan's painting earlier, remember?" Maggie said.

65
00:04:35.729 --> 00:04:38.501
"And she loves cats."

66
00:04:38.502 --> 00:04:41.253
Henry realized Maggie was right.

67
00:04:41.254 --> 00:04:45.891
"Hannah didn't seem to like the painting part of the show," he said.

68
00:04:45.892 --> 00:04:50.693
"But I'm not sure that would make her steal Nathan's painting."

69
00:04:50.694 --> 00:04:55.846
Cole shrugged. "We should probably talk to Hannah, just in case."

70
00:04:55.847 --> 00:04:58.979
"I thought of another suspect," Maggie said.

71
00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:04.661
"That woman with the big sunglasses. She seemed pretty weird."

72
00:05:04.662 --> 00:05:10.010
"True," Henry said. "But why would she steal Nathan's painting?

73
00:05:10.011 --> 00:05:12.502
We don't even know who she is."

74
00:05:12.503 --> 00:05:16.742
"Maybe she's an international art thief." Maggie sounded excited.

75
00:05:16.743 --> 00:05:22.513
"She could be lurking around the show, looking for valuable paintings to steal!"

76
00:05:22.514 --> 00:05:25.355
Henry traded a look with Cole and Nathan.

77
00:05:25.356 --> 00:05:28.677
Maggie liked to exaggerate things sometimes.

78
00:05:28.678 --> 00:05:32.627
"I doubt the woman is a thief," Henry told Maggie.

79
00:05:32.628 --> 00:05:35.311
"But she was acting pretty weird.

80
00:05:35.312 --> 00:05:38.682
I guess we can put her on the list of suspects."

81
00:05:38.683 --> 00:05:43.344
Nathan looked impatient. "So what do we do now?"

82
00:05:43.345 --> 00:05:48.303
"We should find our suspects quickly and question them," Henry said.

83
00:05:48.304 --> 00:05:52.314
Before his friends could answer, the PA system came on.

84
00:05:52.315 --> 00:05:57.578
"I hope you're all enjoying Belltown Arts Day," the mayor's voice said.

85
00:05:57.579 --> 00:06:02.389
"Everyone is very excited to find out the winners of our yearly art show.

86
00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:09.771
The official judging will begin in an hour and a half."
